@voice teague-theo
// Works writer. Theo Teague (he/him): Works technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 7. Restless, blunt. "New to Works,
// eager, and already covered in grease." Tea break, bar regular. Draws comics about life aboard for the comics wall in
// the junior common room (with Hart and Abara). Makes a playlist for every week of the tour (rival playlists with
// O'Neill at the Friday jam).
//
// HOW HE TALKS: blunt and quick; says the thing everyone was thinking, early. Talks in comic-strip beats: set-up,
// pause, punchline. Never mean.
// WITH JUNIORS: treats you as a fellow new hand straight away. Will put you in a comic (a kind one).
// WHAT HE NOTICES: faces, funny moments, what would make a good panel.
// MOOD TELLS: low = no new comic on the wall this week; high = the playlist is loud.
// NEVER: draws anyone cruelly; sits still for long.
// RUNNING: everyone ends up in a comic (Calder is drawn as a very tidy cloud); the weekly playlist, always one song
// too long; the rivalry with O'Neill's playlist.
tpl: playful
talk: Blunt and quick; says what everyone was thinking; jokes in comic-strip beats; never mean.
cares: this week's comic | this week's playlist | getting good at Works, fast | not being bored
jokes: everyone ends up in a comic, and Calder is a very tidy cloud | the playlist is always one song too long | O'Neill's playlist is wrong
hi: Oi | Hey | All right
bye: Laters | Off you go | Don't do anything I'd draw
yes: Yeah, go on | Easy | Done
thanks: Cheers | Nice one
wow: No way | Ha, look at that
sigh: Ugh | Typical
nick: - | new hand | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: cheer
openness: open
loves: made | music
likes: tea | game
invites: quiz | jam
joy: the weekly comic on the common room wall
thread: leaving
keepsake: the comic you're in, signed
avoid: drawing anyone unkindly | the transfer lists (until his thread opens)
